<title>USA: Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are movie ticket sales at the U.S. box office for the July 11-13 weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. on Sunday. Final data will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p> 1 (1) Men in Black ............................ $30.5 million</p>
<p> 2 (*) Contact ................................. $20.6 million</p>
<p> 3 (2) Face/Off ................................ $12.3 million</p>
<p> 4 (4) My Best Friend's Wedding ................  $8.4 million</p>
<p> 5 (3) Hercules ................................  $8.2 million</p>
<p> 6 (6) Out to Sea ..............................  $4.1 million</p>
<p> 7 (5) Batman &amp; Robin ..........................  $3.8 million</p>
<p> 8 (7) Con Air .................................  $2.8 million</p>
<p> 9 (*) A Simple Wish ...........................  $2.6 million</p>
<p> 10(8) The Lost World: Jurassic Park ...........  $1.3 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parentheses. * denotes new release.</p>
<p>&quot;Men in Black&quot; is released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. Sony's TriStar studio released &quot;My Best Friend's Wedding.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Contact&quot; and &quot;Batman &amp; Robin&quot; are released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Face/Off&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Hercules&quot; and &quot;Con Air&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. .</p>
<p>&quot;A Simple Wish&quot; and &quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; are released by Universal Studios, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd. .</p>
<p>&quot;Out to Sea&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
